[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says every report about a wrong date is one bug: the parser reads
dates month first. Reading the reports by tenant, channel and what each one says shows three
problems with three different fixes. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes only the first row. The other two stay open until their own fixes ship.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<SplitTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/2',
    oneDayMove: 'https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/3',
  }}
/>

1. **The parser reads month first** ([#1](https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/1)).
   Every tenant on file writes the day first. A date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day
   and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. It reaches the desk through every channel.
2. **The booking-v3 hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`** ([#2](https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/2)).
   The form reads the date the tenant's way, day first, but tells people to type the month
   first. They do as told, and the date swaps. Same symptom as the parser, different cause:
   only reports sent through a booking-v3 form, and the parser fix does not touch it.
3. **The date moves by one day** ([#3](https://github.com/DawidGaleziewski/mega_backlog/issues/3)).
   Tuesday shows as Monday; a meeting goes out as Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto; an
   invite arrives before the booking. That is time-zone handling, not a swap. The desk had
   already noted these reports as read differently (`desk-notes.json`), but filed them under
   the parser by tenant.

## Why they were merged

The desk merges on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
nobody reads the body. People with all three problems write the same subjects: "Wrong day on
the invite", "Date is wrong". The cause depends on the tenant (its locale and booking form), the
channel, and what the body describes; intake's tag is a guess from the browser and often
disagrees. The table #4471 shows already puts the hint reports apart from the parser:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- When a report about a date comes in, look at the tenant, the channel and the two dates in
  the body before merging: a day/month swap and a one-day move are different tickets.
- The ticket export pages overlap; count each report id once.
- Decision 0001 stays as it is: it is accepted. Replacing it with a rule that reads the cause
  is a new decision record.

